WHAT THIS COVERS

Everything in data/, which is:

  snapshots.csv           market prices recorded by us, with the timestamp
                          of each request
  raw_polls.csv           poll records with the time each first appeared
                          in the source API
  poll_averages.csv       our trailing weighted averages
  poll_probabilities.csv  our conversion of those averages to win
                          probabilities
  poll_history.csv        those averages recomputed at past dates
  race_meta.json          race and candidate mapping

You may share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes with
attribution. Commercial use requires permission: open an issue on the
repository or get in touch.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT AND CANNOT COVER

Individual market prices and poll results are facts, and facts are not
subject to copyright in the United States. This licence applies to the
compilation, the derived figures, and the accompanying documentation, not
to any underlying fact. Anyone is free to collect the same prices from the
same venues.

What is genuinely ours is the combination: market prices and poll-derived
probabilities on a common basis, computed with a conversion fitted and
calibrated against historical races, together with the timestamps recording
when each observation was made and when each poll first became visible.
That combination is not re-derivable from public sources without repeating
the work.

UPSTREAM TERMS

Polling data originates from VoteHub and is licensed CC BY 4.0; that
attribution carries through and is honoured on the site.

Market prices come from public Polymarket and Kalshi endpoints. Their terms
govern your own collection from those venues.

The historical polling error used to calibrate the conversion comes from
FiveThirtyEight's pollster-ratings archive, CC BY 4.0.

